<title>RUSSIA: Russian 168-day T-bill yields 30.13 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 168-day T-bill yields 30.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 168-day discount GKO Treasury bills was 30.13 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had expected the yield between 28.8 and 30.0 percent.</p>
<p>The 22061 series bills, maturing on August 13, 1997, the closest maturity to the new issue, closed at 27.11 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 22061 bills are tax-exempt. The new issue is subject to a 15-percent tax on government securities.</p>
<p>    Series number			     22073</p>
<p>    Issue volume				4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			    5.52 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)			    3.65 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds				    3.21 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			    87.82 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		  87.66 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			    30.13 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield		 30.58 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor					 168 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			     Aug 6, 1997</p>
<p>On February 19 the Finance Ministry raised 4.63 trillion roubles by selling 294-day T-bills (series 22074) making total proceeds from today's auctions 7.84 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It has also repaid about 7.53 trillion roubles in maturing T-bills (series 22043).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
